---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import RateLimiterPlayground from "../../components/lab/RateLimiterPlayground.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Distributed Rate Limiter Visualizer — Lab #03"
    description="Token Bucket vs Leaky Bucket vs Fixed Window vs Sliding Window — animated traffic simulation and a Redis race-condition workbench."
    canonicalURL="https://itsmail.dev/lab/rate-limiter-visualizer"
>
    <main class="lab-detail-page">
        <div class="container">
            <!-- Breadcrumbs & Meta -->
            <div class="lab-top-meta font-mono reveal">
                <a href="/lab" class="back-link" data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.backLink">← // return to lab directory</a>
                <div class="meta-badges">
                    <span class="difficulty-badge badge-medium">● Medium</span>
                    <span class="rfc-badge">RFC 6585 / Redis EVAL</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Header -->
            <header class="lab-header reveal">
                <p class="font-mono text-muted page-eyebrow" data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.eyebrow">// LAB #03 • DISTRIBUTED SYSTEMS</p>
                <h1 class="page-title" data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.title">Distributed Rate Limiter Visualizer</h1>
                <p class="page-lead" data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.subtitle">
                    Inside the algorithms that guard every API on earth: Token Bucket vs Leaky Bucket vs Fixed Window vs Sliding Window — and why naive Redis counters leak past their quota.
                </p>
            </header>

            <!-- Interactive Playground -->
            <section class="playground-section reveal">
                <div class="section-label font-mono">
                    <span class="live-pulse"></span> <span data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.livePlaygroundTitle">LIVE TRAFFIC & CONCURRENCY PLAYGROUND</span>
                </div>
                <RateLimiterPlayground />
            </section>

            <!-- Deep Dive Article -->
            <article class="lab-notes reveal">
                <h2 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Title">1. Why Rate Limiting Exists</h2>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1P1">
                    Every API endpoint has finite CPU, memory, and downstream dependencies. Without a limiter, one misbehaving client can starve every other tenant.
                </p>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1P2">
                    Choosing an algorithm is choosing a trade-off between burst tolerance, memory footprint, and boundary correctness:
                </p>

                <div class="takeaways-grid">
                    <div class="takeaway-card">
                        <span class="takeaway-icon">🪣</span>
                        <h3 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo1Title">Token Bucket</h3>
                        <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo1Desc">A bucket holds up to N tokens and refills at a constant rate. Bursts up to N requests fly through instantly; sustained traffic is paced at the refill rate. Used by Stripe, NGINX, AWS API Gateway.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="takeaway-card">
                        <span class="takeaway-icon">🚰</span>
                        <h3 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo2Title">Leaky Bucket</h3>
                        <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo2Desc">Requests enter a FIFO queue that drains at a fixed rate; overflow is dropped. Shapes traffic into a steady flow — ideal for protecting brittle downstream systems.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="takeaway-card">
                        <span class="takeaway-icon">🪟</span>
                        <h3 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo3Title">Fixed Window</h3>
                        <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo3Desc">A counter resets at fixed intervals. Trivially cheap in Redis (INCR + EXPIRE), but vulnerable to 2× boundary bursts at window edges.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="takeaway-card">
                        <span class="takeaway-icon">🎚️</span>
                        <h3 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo4Title">Sliding Window Log</h3>
                        <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section1Algo4Desc">Stores a timestamp per request and evicts old entries. Boundary-perfect, but O(N) memory per client is expensive at scale.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section2Title">2. The Distributed Cache Problem</h2>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section2P1">
                    The naive pattern — READ value, CHECK quota, WRITE value+1 — is not atomic between thousands of shared workers.
                </p>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section2P2">
                    This is the classic lost-update race condition: 25 concurrent workers against a quota of 10 can let 14 requests sail past. Real incidents cause silent quota bypass and billing discrepancies.
                </p>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section2P3">
                    Fixes: Redis Lua scripts (EVAL), the INCR-then-compare pattern, and distributed locking (SETNX / Redlock).
                </p>

                <h2 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section3Title">3. Production Implementation Patterns</h2>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section3P1">
                    The canonical atomic fixed-window limiter uses INCR-first semantics with a conditional EXPIRE — race-free by construction.
                </p>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section3P2">
                    For sliding-window semantics at scale, production systems use Redis Sorted Sets with ZREMRANGEBYSCORE eviction inside one atomic EVAL.
                </p>

                <div class="defense-box">
                    <div class="defense-title font-mono" data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section3LuaTitle">🛡️ Battle-Tested Patterns:</div>
                    <ul>
                        <li data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section3LuaPoint1"><strong>INCR-first (fixed window):</strong> The incremented ordinal itself is the admission ticket — atomic in one call.</li>
                        <li data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section3LuaPoint2"><strong>Sorted Set + ZREMRANGEBYSCORE (sliding window):</strong> Exact sliding behavior, wrapped in one EVAL for atomicity.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h2 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section4Title">4. The Standard HTTP Contract: IETF RateLimit Headers</h2>
                <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section4P1">
                    The IETF draft-ietf-httpapi-ratelimit-headers standard defines response headers so well-behaved clients can back off automatically:
                </p>

                <div class="headers-guide font-mono">
                    <div class="header-guide-line"><strong data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section4Header1">RateLimit-Limit — total quota per window.</strong></div>
                    <div class="header-guide-line"><strong data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section4Header2">RateLimit-Remaining — room left right now.</strong></div>
                    <div class="header-guide-line"><strong data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section4Header3">RateLimit-Reset — seconds until quota fully recovers.</strong></div>
                    <div class="header-guide-line"><strong data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section4Header4">Retry-After — mandatory on 429 responses.</strong></div>
                </div>

                <h2 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.section5Title">5. Key Takeaways from this Lab</h2>
                <div class="takeaways-grid">
                    <div class="takeaway-card">
                        <span class="takeaway-icon">⚔️</span>
                        <h3 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.takeaway1Title">No limiter survives a race condition</h3>
                        <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.takeaway1Desc">A perfect in-memory algorithm still fails distributed without atomicity. Enforce the read-check-write boundary with INCR-first, Lua EVAL, or locks.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="takeaway-card">
                        <span class="takeaway-icon">📜</span>
                        <h3 data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.takeaway2Title">Algorithm choice is a client contract</h3>
                        <p data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.takeaway2Desc">Token Bucket forgives bursts; Leaky Bucket forgives nothing; Sliding Window tells the truth. Pick what your downstream can absorb, publish via RateLimit headers.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Bottom Navigation -->
            <div class="lab-footer-nav font-mono reveal">
                <a href="/lab/protobuf-wire-inspector" class="lab-nav-btn" data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.footerPrevLab">← Lab #02: Protobuf Wire Inspector</a>
                <span class="next-hint" data-i18n="rateLimiterLab.footerNextHint">Next Lab: OAuth2 PKCE Flow (Sprint 4) →</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    .lab-detail-page {
        padding-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 2.5rem);
        padding-bottom: 6rem;
        min-height: 100vh;
    }

    .lab-top-meta {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }

    .back-link {
        color: var(--cyan, #06b6d4);
        text-decoration: none;
        transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .back-link:hover { color: var(--text, #fff); }

    .meta-badges { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; }

    .difficulty-badge {
        padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
        border-radius: 9999px;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        font-weight: 600;
    }

    .badge-medium {
        background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12);
        color: #f59e0b;
        border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.3);
    }

    .rfc-badge {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
        color: var(--text-muted, #8b949e);
        border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
        border-radius: 9999px;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
    }

    .lab-header { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }

    .page-eyebrow {
        font-size: 0.8125rem;
        color: var(--cyan, #06b6d4);
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .page-title {
        font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        color: var(--text, #fff);
    }

    .page-lead {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        color: var(--text-muted, #8b949e);
        max-width: 48rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .playground-section { margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }

    .section-label {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        color: var(--cyan, #06b6d4);
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .live-pulse {
        width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--green, #00ff88);
        box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--green, #00ff88);
    }

    /* Article Styles */
    .lab-notes {
        max-width: 52rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
        padding-top: 3rem;
        color: var(--text-muted, #8b949e);
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .lab-notes h2 {
        color: var(--text, #fff);
        font-size: 1.35rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .lab-notes p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }

    .takeaways-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
        gap: 1.25rem;
        margin: 1.75rem 0;
    }

    .takeaway-card {
        background: var(--surface, #0d1117);
        border: 1px solid var(--border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
        border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
        padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .takeaway-icon { font-size: 1.5rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }

    .takeaway-card h3 {
        color: var(--text, #fff);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .takeaway-card p {
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        color: var(--text-muted, #8b949e);
        margin: 0;
        line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .defense-box {
        background: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.05);
        border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.25);
        border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
        padding: 1.25rem;
        margin: 1.75rem 0;
    }

    .defense-title {
        color: var(--cyan, #06b6d4);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .defense-box ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    .defense-box li { font-size: 0.82rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    .defense-box li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .defense-box strong { color: var(--text, #fff); }

    .headers-guide {
        background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
        border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
        padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
        margin: 1.5rem 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .header-guide-line { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-muted, #8b949e); }
    .header-guide-line strong { color: #4ade80; font-weight: 600; }

    /* Footer Nav */
    .lab-footer-nav {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
        margin-top: 4rem;
        padding-top: 2rem;
    }

    .lab-nav-btn {
        color: var(--cyan, #06b6d4);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .lab-nav-btn:hover { color: var(--text, #fff); }

    .next-hint { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted, #8b949e); }
</style>
